# Contact form backend (this site has no backend of its own).
# Options:
#   - public/contact-handler.php — a plain PHP script (ships in this repo)
#     that emails submissions directly. Works on any PHP-capable static
#     host; point this at its deployed URL, e.g.
#     https://your-domain.com/contact-handler.php. Currently configured to
#     send to avi.surya@gmail.com for testing — update
#     CONTACT_RECIPIENT_EMAIL in that file before going live.
#   - Formspree (https://formspree.io) or Web3Forms (https://web3forms.com) —
#     easiest to set up, each gives you a POST endpoint URL directly.
#   - A Google Apps Script Web App bound to a Google Sheet, if you want
#     submissions (name, email, phone, reason for contacting) tracked in a
#     Sheet. See scripts/google-apps-script-contact-handler.gs for the
#     script to paste in and deployment steps; paste its /exec URL below.
# Copy this file to .env and fill it in.
PUBLIC_FORM_ENDPOINT=
